&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stratolaunch is a technology accelerator that engineers operationally realistic testing at Mach 5+. Our air-launched, Talon testbeds are reusable, cost-effective platforms that enable routine access to the hypersonic environment. We deliver flight data critical to validating system performance and achieving rapid technology deployment. Together with our customers, we drive innovations that are imperative to advancing national security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stratolaunch is looking for an amazingly talented&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Assistant Facility Security Officer (AFSO)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to join our team! In this role you&amp;nbsp;will assist the Facility Security Officer&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;(FSO) in administering and managing the Security Program, providing policies, plans, procedures, departmental instructions, and technical support of safeguards and security programs to protect client security interests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acts as the chief assistant to the FSO regarding not only implementation of security policy and procedures but also in assisting with the management of other security team members&#39; daily functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversees day-to-day Industrial security facility operations and administering industrial security programs in accordance with the National Industrial Security Program Operating Manual (NISPOM), applicable laws, regulations, and DoD contractual requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages the processing of security clearance paperwork, including collection and review of relevant documents and information for completeness, consistency, and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintains&amp;nbsp;personnel security records and databases, including quality assurance and control of the fingerprinting process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures compliance with all security requirements for the marking, handling, and safeguarding of classified information received and stored within the facility, to include both information and physical security policy and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures program requirements regarding Department of Defense Contract Security Classification Specifications&amp;nbsp;​(DD Form 254s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implements Security Education, Training, and Awareness Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executes visitor control functions to include processing of incoming and outgoing visit requests and verifying incoming visitor identification, prior to allowing access to classified information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verifies&amp;nbsp;preparation of essential reports, troubleshooting industrial security issues, and providing assistance in resolving all concerns and queries from government agencies and company management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
