&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stratolaunch is a technology accelerator that engineers operationally realistic testing at Mach 5+. Our air-launched, Talon testbeds are reusable, cost-effective platforms that enable routine access to the hypersonic environment. We deliver flight data critical to validating system performance and achieving rapid technology deployment. Together with our customers, we drive innovations that are imperative to advancing national security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To help achieve these efforts, Stratolaunch is seeking Industrial Engineer will play a key role in supporting manufacturing operations by optimizing processes, improving production efficiency, and assisting with the implementation and ongoing use of the Manufacturing Execution System (MES). Reporting to the Manufacturing Engineering (ME) Manager, this position will work collaboratively with cross-functional teams to ensure that MES solutions and process improvements align with operational goals. The ideal candidate will bring strong industrial engineering skills, hands-on experience with MES systems, and a continuous improvement mindset to help drive productivity and quality on the shop floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;ESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a cross-functional team by supporting manufacturing process optimization and MES (Manufacturing Execution System) adoption on the production floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the configuration, testing, and deployment of MES solutions in collaboration with the ME Manager and IT teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the integration of MES with existing manufacturing processes, ensuring accurate data capture and process alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate and maintain process documentation, work instructions, and MES user guides to support production teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day MES user support, troubleshooting, and basic training for operators and supervisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze production and MES data to identify process bottlenecks, inefficiencies, and improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply industrial engineering methods such as time studies, workflow analysis, and value stream mapping to optimize manufacturing operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in root-cause analysis of production issues and assist in implementing corrective actions using MES data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with quality, production, and IT teams to ensure MES solutions support quality and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement initiatives, including lean manufacturing projects and kaizen events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the evaluation and implementation of shop floor automation and digital transformation projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical input to the ME Manager and project teams on MES performance, process changes, and improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in project planning and provide schedule and resource inputs as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain regular communication with the ME Manager regarding MES progress, issues, and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate professionalism, integrity, and a commitment to meeting team and organizational goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel, as needed, to support MES rollouts and manufacturing operations at other sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate honesty, responsibility, integrity, and fulfillment of commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
