&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stratolaunch is a technology accelerator that engineers operationally realistic testing at Mach 5+. Our air-launched, Talon testbeds are reusable, cost-effective platforms that enable routine access to the hypersonic environment. We deliver flight data critical to validating system performance and achieving rapid technology deployment. Together with our customers, we drive innovations that are imperative to advancing national security.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Senior Environmental Health and Safety Specialist develops developing and implements EH&amp;amp;S policies, procedures, training, and helps to ensure that the organization complies with all applicable environmental, health and safety regulations. Duties include providing training, conducting inspections and assessments, reviewing training programs, reviewing of policies and procedures, researching regulatory requirements, and handling and managing hazardous waste. A Senior EH&amp;amp;S Specialist may be expected to attain and maintain certain professional certifications and complete continuing training in some areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and develop company EH&amp;amp;S policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand and abide by all company policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and interpret applicable EH&amp;amp;S regulatory requirements, as necessary. This would include those from Cal/OSHA, DOT, EPA, and DTSC, among other federal, state, and local agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support manufacturing and operations teams as an information resource.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct industrial hygiene sampling and exposure analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct injury, incident, and near miss investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct injury/incident trend analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and enforce company EH&amp;amp;S programs, policies, and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct job hazard analyses and area hazard analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support test hazard analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct building and area inspections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide training and safety meetings to manufacturing and operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with inspectors and regulatory agencies as directed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer proficiency, especially with Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, Microsoft Powerpoint, and Adobe Acrobat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience researching and interpreting regulations (e.g. Cal/OSHA, EPA, DOT, Fire Code, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing written programs and company policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong basic mathematical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand or walk 50% of the day or more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any safety or environmental certifications are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EDUCATION &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate degree or higher in EH&amp;amp;S-related field and 8+ years of work experience or 10+ years of work experience in the EH&amp;amp;S field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$47.00-$61.88 hourly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible for up to 10% annual bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
