&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth expertise and experience in deriving and implementing GNC architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability as a technical leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability applying technical expertise to solve high-impact problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills: Capable of conveying complex technical information to diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with relevant industry and military standards and regulatory specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience proposing and leading IRAD projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interact with customers and/or external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience applying analytical and critical thinking skills to solve multi-disciplinary, open-ended engineering problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently in a dynamic environment to achieve business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizen with the ability to obtain a DOW security clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded systems and RTOS / FPGA implementation of algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to derive GNC requirements based on vehicle constraints and mission objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support system sizing and trade study activities based upon mission objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with estimation &amp;amp; data fusion architecture theory and application&lt;/li&gt;
